@startuml
title Sequence Diagram - Submit a Travel Request and Predict Cost (as implemented)

actor Employee
participant "React UI" as UI
participant "API (Node/Express)" as API
participant "Cost Prediction\nService (ML)" as ML
database "Database (Supabase)" as DB

Employee -> UI : complete and submit request\n(origin, destination, class, dates)
UI -> API : POST /api/travel-requests
API -> DB : insert TravelRequest (status=pending)
DB --> API : request id
API -> API : compute days_to_departure\n= start_date - today

API -> ML : POST /predict-cost\n{origin, destination,\ndays_to_departure, travel_class}
alt ML service reachable
  ML -> ML : load model.joblib\nrun RandomForest.predict()
  ML --> API : {predicted_cost, model_version,\ncurrency, duration_hours}
  API -> DB : update TravelRequest.predicted_cost
else ML service unreachable
  API -> API : log warning, continue\n(predicted_cost stays null)
end

DB --> API : updated request
API --> UI : 201 Created (request incl. predicted_cost)
UI --> Employee : show request in list

== later: scoring (separate action) ==
Employee -> UI : click "Score options"
UI -> API : POST /api/travel-requests/:id/score
API -> API : generateOptions()\nbaseline = predicted_cost\n  || estimated_cost || 5000
API -> DB : insert TravelOptions + scores
DB --> API : ok
API --> UI : recommendation + ranked options
UI --> Employee : display recommended option and reason

@enduml
